Summary:  
- The strongest indicator is SpType luminosity class: "V" means dwarf (class 0), "III" or "II" means giant (class 1).  
- Amag is generally brighter (lower) for giants (<14.4) and fainter (>=14.4) for dwarfs.  
- B-V color index tends to be higher for giants (redder colors), but with some overlap.  
- Parallax tends to be smaller for giants (more distant), but not strictly exclusive.  
- Vmag and e_Plx ranges overlap but generally giants have Vmag < 9 and dwarfs > 5.7.

